// Type-checks `src` against the OLDEST Node typings the package supports.
//
// `@types/node` sits at ^22 in devDependencies because vitest@4 peer-requires
// `^20 || ^22 || >=24` and the conflict is not resolvable with `overrides` —
// npm enforces peerOptional ranges against the root's own dependency. That bump
// silently removed a guard: with Node 22 typings in scope, `src` can reference
// a Node 20+ global or API shape and `npm run build` stays green while
// `engines.node` still promises `">=18"`.
//
// This config restores it. CI points `--typeRoots` at a throwaway install of
// `@types/node@^18` so the check runs without disturbing the real dependency
// tree; see the `node18-typings` job. `noEmit` because only the diagnostics
// matter, and `declaration: false` because it cannot be combined with `noEmit`.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.build.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "declaration": false,
    "types": ["node"]
  }
}
